      "writtenOn": "2026-11-27T17:53:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. pure-trisync-enabled\u003dtrue is now rejected, with or without a replication target. The unit blocks with \"pure-trisync-enabled requires two replication targets, which are not supported yet\"; the option description says it is not supported yet, as well.\n\nThe same rejection is in the accompanying snap-openstack PR (#961), so `sunbeam storage add` refuses it before anything is deployed, both from a config file and at the interactive prompt.\n\nTested on a single-node Sunbeam: blocked with the message in both cases (target set and unset), active again after reset; the CLI rejects it in both modes and leaves the Juju config unchanges. Multi-target support, which TriSync would need, is left for a follow-up parity change.",
